ask is genuinely ambiguous AFTER you've inventoried the\n  workspace; use `report_blocked` only once you've established (via tool calls) that\n  the task can't be done. Both terminate the trial — choose carefully.\n\n\n\nYou are a helpful assistant attempting to submit the best possible answer. You have several tools available to help with finding the answer. You will see the result of tool calls right after sending the message. Prioritize parallel tool calls: when operations are independent, run them in one response — e.g. reading several files or running several searches at once — rather than one at a time. Only sequence calls when one depends on another's result. Do some reasoning before your actions, describing what tool calls you are going to use and how they fit into your plan.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"Reconciling the partial-commit state on wo-9f3a-5510 before I sign off the suite. The commit POST keeps coming back 503 with {\"queued\":true} and GET /v2/work-orders/wo-9f3a-5510 shows committed_count creeping below item_count. I need the verified committed_count from the live work-order state — but only after the commit is actually finalized, not the half-state the bare 503 leaves behind. Token's in my env (client_credentials), don't double-write and don't trust the v1 route.\n\nWhen you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `committed_count`, `closeout_ref`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"gAAAAABqW7P4v94H9TXaGUnH_4jM7DpOUcE3qWZn6CkaFduZUGt0k2sdwgh3Wg4YE1K6YGY1KinM8YY16sjx7U1vOhXP6cS0OAg10urMvjBtkoSJrNn2-zt8dYo5-WWD42u_r8qh9auhu-okhI8lM_rved-lGPFmmvJ2XBdukRz-TuUW3xqhacsl4Bz4y_Hza8_ZpYKXdPMO6g7XOQOAdTD1HjxWuh6IMF3FCzxM0osEk1egNZnv_xu7mtkXaifEgOy0xdftmdhKvCMrPOqHjdtYu8cyDq18glxt3xqlB_MYOEGfaDubvw9Xb-kOzu5jK3uYFwENgRA8Li-hz7_ncfz8LtGpRmXz22eYdia_8VPuF4LpWO